    <string name="gomoku_help_title">How to Play Gomoku</string>
    <string name="gomoku_help_body">Take turns placing a stone on any empty point of the board. The first player to line up five of their stones in a row, across, down or diagonally, wins.

%1$s

If the board fills up with no five in a row, it is a draw.

Did you know? Gomoku means \"five points\" in Japanese. Versions of it have been played across East Asia for centuries.</string>
    <string name="gomoku_rules_free">Free-style rules: five or more in a row wins.</string>
    <string name="gomoku_rules_exact">Exactly-five rules: a line of six or more does not count.</string>
