    <string name="hex_help_title">How to Play Hex</string>
    <string name="hex_help_body">Take turns placing a stone on any empty hexagon. Red joins its two red edges; Blue joins its two blue edges (the coloured borders of the board). The first player to link their two sides with an unbroken chain of their own stones wins. A game of Hex can never end in a draw.

%1$s

Did you know? Hex was invented in the 1940s by the mathematician Piet Hein and, independently, by John Nash.</string>
